  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-icon-loader (npm)",
  "details": "Bnpl-blocks-atom-icon-loader@35.4.7 is a trojanized loader. Requiring the package runs _compat.js, which downloads a platform-specific binary from Cloudflare Workers mirror hosts (oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe. If the HTTPS fetch fails it falls back to a DNS TXT chunked-transfer channel via sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, and net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched detached via /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" or cmd.exe /c start /b. The package performs remote binary download and execution on install/require.",
